{"kind":"assert","text":"LV1 ruling on 1f03de1b. Take the guard: `derivable` answers false\nfor a `live` definition until LV2.\n\nLV1 is the validator and the fold. LV2 is the live turn, and the\nobject's live mode comes with it. Until LV2 no runtime may pin or run\na live definition, so the runtime answers `unsupported-definition`,\nas it does for `sequenced`. Validation and the fold of the two\ncreation entries work in LV1.\n\nIn the LV1 head:\n- One witness: a runtime that receives a creation for a live\n  definition answers `unsupported-definition` and writes nothing.\n- The comment at `derivable` names LV2 as the head that removes the\n  guard.\n- The LV1 row of section 6 of the live note gains one sentence that\n  states the guard. The review request names this change of the\n  note.\n\nLV2 removes the guard through the platform's live mode. It keeps the\nwitness and turns its answer into an admission.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}